# "For each of those creatures, create a Monster Role token attached to it" is one instruction (CR 101.4): the two Roles are
# created together, as one event (CR 603.2c). Kambal's "whenever one or more tokens you control enter, each opponent loses 1 life
# and you gain 1 life" triggers once for both: Bot2 at 19, Bot1 at 21.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Memnite x2
Kambal, Profiteering Mayor
Become Brutes
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Kambal, Profiteering Mayor.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Become Brutes.Cast
Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite#1; Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite#2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite#1.Power = 2
? Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite#2.Power = 2

[Expect]
Stack.Count = 0
Attached = Monster > Memnite; Monster > Memnite
Bot2.Life = 19
Bot1.Life = 21
